State of the build
• The harness verified the build at session start. The binary answers a -p prompt correctly.
• The last 4 evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs passed. There are no reverts in the 10-session window.
• Two files are close to the size limit in tests/module_size.rs, and going past it makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task:
  • src/help.rs is 10 lines away. Any task that edits help text has to update its size entry in the same diff.
  • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines and has no entry. It's 14 lines away.

What I found and suggest the planner pick up
1. #1144 item 2 (filed by @yuanhao, not started). yoyo still keeps its own hand-written Claude limits in commands_info.rs:767 (it still says sonnet-4-5 has a 1M window) and agent_builder.rs:1341 (anthropic_output_maximum). yoagent 0.27.2's price table now supplies these limits. Removing them should also close the last open part of #1121. I confirmed that anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 on Bedrock still runs on guessed limits (200000 context, max_tokens 16000).
   • Probe tip: that warning only shows when you run from /tmp. Run from the repo root, it didn't show, probably because this repo's .yoyo.toml sets those limits.
2. Known-model lists for other providers. The new test that catches made-up model names only checks names containing claude. Five other offered names look suspicious but are unverified: o4-mini-high, mixtral-8x7b-32768, grok-2, gpt-5.5-mini, MiniMax-M1-40k.
3. #1127. Eight shell commands still print REPL /slash syntax. The fix is mechanical and there's a pattern to copy, but it touches help.rs, so it hits the size limit above.

